      "content": "I can certainly sharpen that point to make the impact more direct while keeping it professional. You might want to frame the lateness as a disruption to the team's \"morning rhythm,\" which is crucial for our collective efficiency.\n\nHere is the revised section you can insert or use as a replacement:\n\n\"However, we need to address a specific friction point: your frequent lateness to the morning stand-ups. While your client retention is stellar, arriving late disrupts the team's momentum before we've even started the day. When you're not there at the start, the rest of us have to fill the gap, which slows down our overall workflow and creates a bottleneck. We need you to be punctual not just for your own sake, but to ensure you aren't inadvertently holding back the entire group. Let's set a firm expectation that your presence at 9:00 AM sharp is non-negotiable to support the team's speed.\"\n\nLet me know if you want to add any more specific examples of how the delay affected the team!",
